NGINX: NGINX (pronounced "Engine-X") is a high-performance web server, reverse proxy server, load balancer, and HTTP cache.

It is one of the most widely used web servers in the world and is used by companies such as Netflix, Airbnb, and Cloudflare.

What Does NGINX Do?
===================

		1. Web Server
				When it added module php-fpm then it will server wp.
					( Wordpress =  webserver + Php + Mariadb )
					
		2. Load Balancer

			NGINX can distribute traffic across multiple servers.
			
					   NGINX
						 |
				  +------+------+ 
				  |      |      |
				Web1   Web2   Web3				
						
	
		
		3. Reverse Proxy  NGINX sits in front of application servers and forwards requests to them.
					Client
					   |
					   v
					 NGINX
					   |
					   +--> App Server 1
					   +--> App Server 2		
		
Example:

	Client --> NGINX --> Node.js Application		
		
	Proxy :  
				1)  Forward 
				2)  Reverse Proxy 


		4. Caching
				
		NGINX can store frequently requested content and serve it directly.

			Client Request
				  |
			   NGINX Cache
				  |
			  Cached Response
				
		Result:

			Faster websites
			Lower backend load			
				
NGINX Architecture
==================
Unlike traditional web servers that create one process per connection, NGINX uses an event-driven architecture.				
				
	           Master Process
                  |
        +---------+---------+
        |         |         |
     Worker1   Worker2   Worker3
	 
	 
Advantages:

	Low memory usage
	Handles thousands of connections
	High performance
	
	
